NOTICE — third-party code and specifications

This project vendors no third-party source. Two files sit near CPython and
neither one copies it:

  * src/shell.zig REIMPLEMENTS POSIX shell word-splitting semantics (quoting,
    escapes, operators, assignment prefixes, pipelines) from the POSIX shell
    command language specification and from observed shell behaviour. No CPython
    source was copied, translated, or transliterated into it. Where it agrees
    with Python's `shlex`, the agreement is about what a shell does.

  * tests/shlex_oracle.py CALLS the Python standard library's `shlex` module as a
    differential oracle at test time and records what it returns. `shlex` is not
    vendored, redistributed, or shipped; the script imports it the way any Python
    program imports the stdlib, runs only under `zig build parity`, and is not
    part of either binary.

    src/testdata/shell-oracle.jsonl is the OUTPUT of running that script over
    this project's own corpus (src/testdata/shell-corpus.txt) — data about
    behaviour, generated from inputs written here.

Consequently no Python Software Foundation licence terms attach to the binaries
this project builds. The PSF licence governs a CPython installation, which is a
prerequisite of the test suite in the same way a C compiler is a prerequisite of
a C project.
